So contactless smart card is a smart card that uses inductive coupling to communicate with its reader.

4
00:00:16,329 --> 00:00:23,590
Inductive coupling in fact, is the technology behind NFC, near-field communication, and short range

5
00:00:23,590 --> 00:00:30,340
RFID for for radio frequency identification in the 1350 six megahertz radio band.

6
00:00:30,370 --> 00:00:40,120
So high frequency radio band proximity contactless smart cards are defined by the ISO 14,443 set of

7
00:00:40,120 --> 00:00:41,680
international standards.

8
00:00:42,130 --> 00:00:46,780
The ISO 14,443 is divided into four layers.

9
00:00:46,930 --> 00:00:55,900
The upper layers, which is ISO 14,443 four, specifies the contactless transport protocol, sometimes

10
00:00:55,900 --> 00:01:00,850
referred to as T equal CL, CL for contactless.

11
00:01:01,150 --> 00:01:07,660
The application layer that comes on top of the contactless protocol is supposed to be the very same

