ISO 7008 16 dash four that comes on top of the T equals zero or t equal one.

13
00:01:13,540 --> 00:01:15,070
Transport protocols.

14
00:01:18,730 --> 00:01:28,390
As you can see here, I put some example of the contactless technology like car keys, passports, bags,

15
00:01:28,390 --> 00:01:37,090
identification or bags, tags, transport, uh, cars, transportation or like medicine tax.

16
00:01:44,940 --> 00:01:52,440
So a lot of contactless cards on the market today are not smart cards, but wired logic memories with

17
00:01:52,440 --> 00:01:53,550
an RF interface.

18
00:01:53,970 --> 00:02:01,980
So the marketing gives them different names like RFID labels, NFC tags, contactless tickets, but

19
00:02:01,980 --> 00:02:07,740
they are all based on the same physical principle inductive coupling at 1350 six megahertz.

20
00:02:07,740 --> 00:02:13,110
Please remember always that here when we talk about the contactless communication, we are in the range

21
00:02:13,110 --> 00:02:14,940
of the 1350 six megahertz.

22
00:02:14,940 --> 00:02:24,270
This is the frequency that characterizes that characterize this technology and are all compliant with

23
00:02:24,270 --> 00:02:32,910
either ISO 14,143 standard for proximity cards, or ISO 15 15,693 standard for vicinity cards.

24
00:02:39,210 --> 00:02:46,170
So here we will be talking about the coupling device or coupler, or let's say the reader.

25
00:02:46,170 --> 00:02:53,070
Now that we know that a smart card is basically a secure microcontroller communicating with the external

26
00:02:53,070 --> 00:03:00,330
world through a serial line, we must find a better name than reader for the device that ensures the

27
00:03:00,330 --> 00:03:03,630
connectivity and gives access to the smart card instructions.

28
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:12,240
Even if the term smart card reader has been popularized by the Pcsc and Ccid specifications, it does

29
00:03:12,240 --> 00:03:19,710
not reflect the technical reality, because a card's instruction set opens lots more features than just

30
00:03:19,710 --> 00:03:20,760
reading some data.

31
00:03:21,630 --> 00:03:29,640
Reading a smart card makes not more sense than reading a remote web server or reading an SQL database.

32
00:03:29,910 --> 00:03:31,860
You do not read a raw memory.

33
00:03:31,860 --> 00:03:38,340
In fact, your application sends some commands to get authenticated since other commands to explore

34
00:03:38,340 --> 00:03:44,190
a file system sends commands also to insert or update or delete the data.

35
00:03:44,190 --> 00:03:47,370
Or read it, of course, but not only.

36
00:03:47,910 --> 00:03:55,080
Therefore, the device in which the smart card is inserted plays the role of a pass through gateway

37
00:03:55,080 --> 00:04:01,230
between a software running in the host computer or host terminal, and the software running inside the

38
00:04:01,230 --> 00:04:02,760
card's microcontroller.

39
00:04:03,780 --> 00:04:11,070
This pass through gateway translates commands coming from the host application through either USB,

40
00:04:11,250 --> 00:04:19,019
serial Ethernet, or any other computer interconnection technology into electronic signals that are

41
00:04:19,019 --> 00:04:21,690
compliant with the asynchronous half duplex.

42
00:04:21,690 --> 00:04:29,340
Serial T equals zero or T equal one transport protocol, but this gateway does not add any processing

43
00:04:29,340 --> 00:04:29,970
logic.

44
00:04:29,970 --> 00:04:33,630
Its position is to couple the smart card with the computer.

45
00:04:34,170 --> 00:04:43,350
As a consequence, the standard name as defined by the ISO 7816 is coupling device CD or simply a coupler.

46
00:04:43,770 --> 00:04:53,700
Contactless coupler are in turn named Proximity Coupling Device or PCD by the ISO 14,443 or vicinity

47
00:04:53,700 --> 00:04:58,320
coupling device vxd by the ISO 15,693.

48
00:05:02,050 --> 00:05:04,660
So we were talking about the PCD.

49
00:05:05,500 --> 00:05:08,470
Now we will be talking about the Picc components.

50
00:05:09,070 --> 00:05:15,190
As you can see here in this picture, the card and the reader unit communicates with each other through

51
00:05:15,190 --> 00:05:18,610
125kHz radio frequency fields.

52
00:05:18,700 --> 00:05:28,840
So 30 56MHz for the contactless smart card cards by a process called resonant energy transfer.

53
00:05:29,320 --> 00:05:34,300
Passive cards have three components which are sealed inside the plastic.

54
00:05:36,810 --> 00:05:46,770
Inside the plastic, we have an antenna consisting of a coil of of wire, a capacitor and integrated

55
00:05:46,770 --> 00:05:47,490
circuit.

56
00:05:47,490 --> 00:05:53,880
So as I said, the the course is is composed by three components, as you can see here in the picture.

57
00:05:55,680 --> 00:06:05,220
So as I said it contains an antenna consisted of a coil of wire, a capacitor and integrated circuit

58
00:06:05,220 --> 00:06:10,650
which contains the user's ID number in specific formats and no other data.

59
00:06:10,980 --> 00:06:16,980
The reader has its own antenna, which continuously transmits a short range radio frequency field.

60
00:06:17,880 --> 00:06:24,390
When the card is placed within range of the reader, the antenna coil and capacitor, which form a tuned

61
00:06:24,390 --> 00:06:31,770
circuit absorb and store energy from the field, resonating at the frequency emitted by the reader.

62
00:06:32,430 --> 00:06:37,080
This energy is rectified to direct current, which powers the integrated circuit.

63
00:06:37,410 --> 00:06:45,570
The chip sends its ID number or other data to the antenna coil, which transmits it by radio frequency

64
00:06:45,570 --> 00:06:47,490
signals back to the reader unit.

65
00:06:48,150 --> 00:06:54,090
The reader checks whether the ID number from the card is correct, and then performs whatever function

66
00:06:54,090 --> 00:06:56,610
it has been programmed to do for that ID number.

67
00:06:57,150 --> 00:07:04,650
All the energy to power the card comes from the reader unit, so passive cards must be close to a reader

68
00:07:04,650 --> 00:07:06,030
to transmit their data.

69
00:07:11,590 --> 00:07:17,320
So the first part here we will be talking on how the card is fabricated.

70
00:07:17,320 --> 00:07:22,870
So the exchange of information between the contactless card and the associated reader is completely

71
00:07:22,870 --> 00:07:29,320
accomplished by remote electromagnetic coupling between an antenna lodged in the contactless card and

72
00:07:29,320 --> 00:07:35,680
the second antenna located in the reader for developing, storing and processing the information.

73
00:07:35,680 --> 00:07:41,890
The card is equipped with a contactless chip or electronic module which is connected to the antenna.

74
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:49,450
The antenna and the chip or contactless module are typically located on a dielectric.

75
00:07:49,450 --> 00:07:58,060
Dielectric support made of plastic material can be PVC, polyester, polycarbonate, etc. the antenna

76
00:07:58,060 --> 00:08:05,170
here is obtained by chemical, copper or aluminium etching on the support or winding or winding of conductive

77
00:08:05,170 --> 00:08:09,790
metal wire, such as a copper.

78
00:08:09,790 --> 00:08:11,710
The card is often monoblock.

79
00:08:11,710 --> 00:08:20,890
The antenna support is inserted between two layers of plastic materials PVC, Pet, PC, etc., forming

80
00:08:20,890 --> 00:08:26,530
the upper and lower card bodies and then heat bonded by hot lamination under pressure.

81
00:08:26,800 --> 00:08:34,390
The contactless chip or module is connected to the antenna by an electrically conductive glue or equivalent,

82
00:08:34,390 --> 00:08:37,690
which enables the ohmic contact to be established.

83
00:08:40,900 --> 00:08:42,549
So here we are in the summary.

84
